From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: the launcher button never shows Google's "G"

With a keyboard ChromeOS takes for one with Google's newest launcher key
(split modifiers: a function key and a Quick Insert key, as on recent
Chromebooks), the shelf's launcher button shows the "G"-shaped launcher
icon (kCampbellHeroIcon) instead of ChromeOS's circle. Seen on the NVIDIA test PC
with 16852.17.4 (Chrome 157.0.8103.31; 8103.22 didn't), most likely from
the test tool's virtual keyboard, which reports every key. NickelOS's
launcher button is ChromeOS's own circle on every keyboard.

---
diff --git a/ash/shelf/home_button.cc b/ash/shelf/home_button.cc
index 7fddb4c..116798e 100644
--- a/ash/shelf/home_button.cc
+++ b/ash/shelf/home_button.cc
@@ -259,8 +259,11 @@ class HomeButton::ButtonImageView : public views::View {
   }
 
   void UpdateIconImageModel() {
-    if (Shell::Get()->keyboard_capability()->GetMetaKeyToDisplay() ==
-        ui::mojom::MetaKey::kLauncherRefresh) {
+    // NickelOS: always ChromeOS's own launcher button, never the Google "G"
+    // ChromeOS shows for keyboards with Google's newest launcher key.
+    if ((false) &&
+        Shell::Get()->keyboard_capability()->GetMetaKeyToDisplay() ==
+            ui::mojom::MetaKey::kLauncherRefresh) {
       image_model_ =
           ui::ImageModel::FromVectorIcon(kCampbellHeroIcon, GetIconColorId());
     } else {
